#. macro: <sheet ClassJob $n2 0> — a value from a game data sheet, such as a name; sheet = ClassJob, row = number parameter 2, column = 0 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($n2 == 14)>an <sheet ClassJob $n2 0><else><if ($n2 == 5)>an <sheet ClassJob $n2 0><else><if ($n2 == 26)>an <sheet ClassJob $n2 0><else><if ($n2 == 33)>an <… — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 2 == 14 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
